<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Askar Akayev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Askar Akayev is a Kyrgyz physicist who was elected president of the Kirghiz SSR in 1990 and led Kyrgyzstan to independence in 1991. Seen at first as a reformer, he became increasingly authoritarian. He was overthrown in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tulip-revolution">Tulip Revolution</a> of March 2005 and went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p></div>
